      "sequence_position": 12,
      "problem": "Calculate \n${\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,-5,\\,-6⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,-9,\\,8⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-5,\\,-6⟩-⟨-2,\\,-9,\\,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,4,\\,-14⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
